1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,850
Workflow Puzzle Lab — learn to build AI workflows that don't fall over

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,850
8 puzzles · beginner → advanced

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,850
Runs fully offline in mock AI mode — no API key, no backend

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,850
Reviewer guide: one click jumps to any capability, failure pre-armed

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,350
Every puzzle opens with objective, expected output, and completion goals

6
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:30,850
The loop: understand → run → break → repair → prove

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,350
The starting workflow is naive on purpose: input → AI → output

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,850
Run it clean first

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,350
80 / 100 · Resilient

10
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:52,850
Now inject a controlled failure — deterministic, repeats every run

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,350
The model wraps its answer in markdown chatter

12
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,850
It says completed. Green checkmarks. And it shipped invalid data.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,350
Output integrity 0 / 20 — the most dangerous failure mode

14
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,850
Nothing in this design was watching for it

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,225
Add a Validator between the model and the output

16
00:01:19,375 --> 00:01:23,600
It checks the output against a schema, then escalates

17
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:27,975
41 → 100 (+59) · one retry fixed the formatting fluke

18
00:01:28,125 --> 00:01:32,350
The AI step recovered — the trace shows both attempts

19
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,725
Different failure: a missing owner, on every attempt

20
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:41,100
Retrying can't fix it — so it stopped safely instead

21
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:45,475
Repair handles what retrying can't

22
00:01:45,625 --> 00:01:49,850
Solved · all three goals met

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,475
Some failures no schema can catch

24
00:01:55,625 --> 00:02:01,100
Put a human in front of the send step

25
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:06,725
The run pauses before anything leaves the building

26
00:02:06,875 --> 00:02:12,350
It guarantees this will never recur and refunds a full year

27
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:17,975
Approve, edit, or reject — edits are schema-checked live

28
00:02:18,125 --> 00:02:23,600
Every decision, with its note, lands in the trace

29
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:29,225
And a rejection is respected

30
00:02:29,375 --> 00:02:34,850
Stopped safely at 87. The send step never ran.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,225
The flagship model times out

32
00:02:39,375 --> 00:02:43,600
One timeout, whole run dead

33
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:47,975
Give it a bounded retry budget

34
00:02:48,125 --> 00:02:52,350
Retries ride out a brownout — the trace shows all three attempts

35
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:56,725
Now the model is down hard

36
00:02:56,875 --> 00:03:01,100
Retries just hammer a dead service

37
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:05,475
So fall back to a smaller model that's actually up

38
00:03:05,625 --> 00:03:09,850
A plainer answer that still passes the schema

39
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:17,350
A solar flare kills the pipeline mid-run

40
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:24,850
But a checkpoint saved every completed step

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:32,350
Three steps restored, not re-executed — it continues where it died

42
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:39,850
An interruption becomes a pause, not a restart

43
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,850
Every run is scored: outcome, integrity, chaos handling, design hygiene

44
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,850
What survived — and what's still fragile in the design

45
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,850
All of this ran offline in mock mode

46
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,850
A real model is optional, never required

47
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,850
Eight puzzles. Retries, fallbacks, validation, human review, resume.
